                     change to promote membrane insertion of SecA/bound
                     preprotein; ATP hydrolysis appears to drive release of the
                     preprotein from SecA and deinsertion of SecA from the
                     membrane; additional proteins SecD/F/YajC aid SecA
                     recycling; exists in an equilibrium between monomers and
                     dimers; may possibly form higher order oligomers; in some
                     organisms, especially gram positive pathogens, have
                     paralogs that have been found to be nonessential but do
                     function in secretion of a subset of exported proteins"
                     /codon_start=1
                     /transl_table=11
                     /product="preprotein translocase subunit SecA"
                     /protein_id="NP_647387.1"
